import{_ as a,o as t,c as i,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 216 | Four Sacred-Cultivation Realms General Discussion: Qualitative-Lever Leaps of Dao Integration / Boundary-Breaking / World-Creation / Origin","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 216 | Four Sacred-Cultivation Realms General Discussion: Qualitative-Lever Leaps of Dao Integration / Boundary-Breaking / World-Creation / Origin","no":216,"module":1,"tags":["Realm","Four Sacred-Cultivation Realms","General Discussion","Qualitative-Lever Leap"],"related":["14-Unified Cultivation Realm Classification","17-Plane Transcendent Standards","03-Symbiotic Civilization Charter"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0216_模块1-圣修四境总论-质变飞跃.md","filePath":"en/0216_模块1-圣修四境总论-质变飞跃.md"}'),r={name:"en/0216_模块1-圣修四境总论-质变飞跃.md"};function o(s,e,l,u,c,d){return t(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-216-four-sacred-cultivation-realms-general-discussion-qualitative-lever-leaps-of-dao-integration-boundary-breaking-world-creation-origin" tabindex="-1">Entry 216 | Four Sacred-Cultivation Realms General Discussion: Qualitative-Lever Leaps of Dao Integration / Boundary-Breaking / World-Creation / Origin <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-216-four-sacred-cultivation-realms-general-discussion-qualitative-lever-leaps-of-dao-integration-boundary-breaking-world-creation-origin" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 216 | Four Sacred-Cultivation Realms General Discussion: Qualitative-Lever Leaps of Dao Integration / Boundary-Breaking / World-Creation / Origin&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 1 · In-Depth Realm Refinement | Baseline references: Documents 14, 17, 03</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-from-law-users-to-law-co-builders" tabindex="-1">Introduction: From law users to law co-builders <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-from-law-users-to-law-co-builders" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: From law users to law co-builders&quot;">​</a></h2><p>In Heng Yuan Zhou (Wanling Hengmao Origin Cosmos)&#39;s nine-realm system, the last four realms — Dao Integration, Boundary-Breaking, World-Creation, Origin — are collectively called the &quot;four sacred-cultivation realms.&quot; Unlike the five mortal-cultivation realms&#39; gradual cognitive upgrade, every one of the four sacred-cultivation realms is a <strong>cosmic-level qualitative leap</strong>: cultivators rise from &quot;understanding and using laws&quot; to &quot;participating in law creation, rewriting, and guarding.&quot; These four realms are not quantitative accumulation, but fundamental identity shift — from the cosmos&#39;s &quot;tenant&quot; to the cosmos&#39;s &quot;co-builder.&quot;</p><p>The six top-level axioms manifest the most concentrated constraint in the four sacred-cultivation realms: the anti-predation axiom requires sacred strong ones not use law permissions to prey on beings; the republican axiom of Myriad Races requires sacred strong ones&#39; power to serve Myriad Races not be privately hoarded; the collective ascension axiom requires sacred strong ones to lift Myriad Races along, not ascend alone; the causal self-discipline axiom&#39;s constraint on cross-plane operations is strictest at the sacred-cultivation stage; the law-first axiom ensures the four sacred-cultivation realms&#39; law definitions are stable, not inflated by plot needs; the universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><p>This entry discusses the four sacred-cultivation realms&#39; qualitative-leap logic in general: what is the qualitative-leap core of each realm? Why are these four realms &quot;sacred&quot; not &quot;mortal&quot;?</p><h2 id="i-qualitative-leap-map-of-the-four-sacred-cultivation-realms" tabindex="-1">I. Qualitative-Leap Map of the Four Sacred-Cultivation Realms <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-qualitative-leap-map-of-the-four-sacred-cultivation-realms" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Qualitative-Leap Map of the Four Sacred-Cultivation Realms&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Realm</th><th>Qualitative-Leap Core</th><th>Identity Shift</th><th>Power Tier</th><th>Social Role</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dao Integration Realm</td><td>Personal Dao merges into the cosmic law network</td><td>From &quot;using laws&quot; to &quot;integrating with laws&quot;</td><td>Law-level</td><td>Grandmaster</td></tr><tr><td>Boundary-Breaking Realm</td><td>Breaking through plane barriers&#39; law constraints</td><td>From &quot;intra-plane&quot; to &quot;cross-plane&quot;</td><td>Plane-level</td><td>Plane strong one</td></tr><tr><td>World-Creation Realm</td><td>Weaving laws in isolated space, creating worlds</td><td>From &quot;user&quot; to &quot;creator&quot;</td><td>World-level</td><td>World-creator</td></tr><tr><td>Origin Realm</td><td>Touching cosmic origin, participating in law fine-tuning</td><td>From &quot;intra-world&quot; to &quot;origin layer&quot;</td><td>Cosmic-level</td><td>Plane Transcendent</td></tr></tbody></table><p>These four realms&#39; qualitative leap is not quantitative like &quot;more energy, stronger magic power,&quot; but <strong>existence-dimensional leap</strong> — every realm means the cultivator&#39;s &quot;existence&quot; expands to a new dimensional layer.</p><h2 id="ii-dao-integration-realm-first-qualitative-leap-of-heaven-human-unity" tabindex="-1">II. Dao Integration Realm: First Qualitative Leap of Heaven-Human Unity <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-dao-integration-realm-first-qualitative-leap-of-heaven-human-unity" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Dao Integration Realm: First Qualitative Leap of Heaven-Human Unity&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Dao Integration Realm is the watershed between mortal and sacred cultivation. A Dao Origin cultivator has already formed personal Dao, but this Dao is still &quot;personal&quot;; Dao Integration requires personal Dao to deeply fuse with cosmic origin laws, reaching the state where &quot;every move is in accord with Dao.&quot;</p><p>The core marker of this qualitative leap is: the cultivator no longer needs to &quot;deliberately&quot; use laws; laws themselves are his natural extension. He can rewrite local laws&#39; operation within a wide range; life form begins evolving to higher dimensions, partially shedding material body constraints. Dao Integration strong ones can create stable personal law domains, the first expansion from &quot;personal power&quot; to &quot;law space.&quot;</p><p>In the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, breaking through to Dao Integration must pass Standards Committee assessment, in which the mind-state dimension takes 25% — it is not enough that power reaches Dao Integration; <strong>the Dao heart must be in sync with symbiotic ideals</strong>. A cultivator harboring predation, even if power reaches Dao Integration standards, will have their &quot;Dao&quot; reject cosmic symbiotic laws and cannot truly integrate.</p><h2 id="iii-boundary-breaking-realm-breaking-through-plane-barriers" tabindex="-1">III. Boundary-Breaking Realm: Breaking Through Plane Barriers <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-boundary-breaking-realm-breaking-through-plane-barriers" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Boundary-Breaking Realm: Breaking Through Plane Barriers&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Boundary-Breaking Realm&#39;s qualitative-leap core is <strong>cross-plane operation capability</strong>. Before Dao Integration, no matter how strong a cultivator is, they are constrained by their plane&#39;s laws; Boundary-Breaking cultivators can break through plane membrane limits and travel cross-plane without anchor support.</p><p>This leap&#39;s meaning far exceeds &quot;travel capability&quot; — it means the cultivator&#39;s existence is no longer confined to a single law system. Boundary-Breaking strong ones can operate plane membranes: opening channels, repairing cracks, monitoring plane fluctuations. They are bridges and guardians between planes.</p><p>The causal self-discipline axiom reaches its strictest in this realm: cross-plane operations must be strictly filed, observe first then limited interference, return knowledge only not disturb karma. Boundary-Breaking strong ones violating this principle will be immediately intervened by the Alaya Network, restricting cross-plane permissions — because cross-plane disturbance consequences may affect the entire plane chain&#39;s karmic stability.</p><h2 id="iv-world-creation-realm-law-weaving-and-small-world-creation" tabindex="-1">IV. World-Creation Realm: Law Weaving and Small-World Creation <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-world-creation-realm-law-weaving-and-small-world-creation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. World-Creation Realm: Law Weaving and Small-World Creation&quot;">​</a></h2><p>World-Creation Realm is the most creativity-concentrated of the four sacred-cultivation realms. Cultivators can create complete worlds in isolated space — including matter, energy, laws, life. This is not &quot;creating from nothing,&quot; but <strong>weaving a self-consistent law system per cosmic laws&#39; bottom logic</strong>, turning isolated space from &quot;blank&quot; into &quot;world.&quot;</p><p>World-Creation&#39;s qualitative leap lies in: cultivators turn from &quot;law users&quot; into &quot;law designers.&quot; The world they design must satisfy the law-first axiom — self-consistent, stable, expandable. A world with non-self-consistent laws collapses on its own during creation; this is why World-Creation breakthroughs are extremely rare: not insufficient power, but insufficient design ability.</p><p>In the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, worlds created by World-Creation strong ones are not private property but civilization&#39;s public resources — usable as cultivation resource zones, experimental sites, civilizational sanctuaries, new-race cultivation zones. Creators have guardianship responsibility for their created worlds, but no monopoly rights.</p><h2 id="v-origin-realm-cosmic-level-being-and-plane-transcendent-threshold" tabindex="-1">V. Origin Realm: Cosmic-Level Being and Plane Transcendent Threshold <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-origin-realm-cosmic-level-being-and-plane-transcendent-threshold" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Origin Realm: Cosmic-Level Being and Plane Transcendent Threshold&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Origin Realm is the nine-realm system&#39;s apex. Touching cosmic origin laws, understanding the cosmos&#39;s ultimate operating rules, able to participate in cosmic law fine-tuning and optimization. Life form deeply connects with cosmic origin, near-immortal.</p><p>Origin Realm strong ones are &quot;Plane Transcendents,&quot; rated by the four-dimensional assessment system: strength 40%, mind 25%, contribution 20%, responsibility 15%. This is not a power ranking, but <strong>responsibility certification</strong> — only cultivators meeting all four-dimensional standards qualify to participate in cosmic law fine-tuning.</p><p>Origin Realm is not the endpoint. In the extended setting (pending Terminology Committee calibration), above Origin Realm are also the Multiverse Realm (multi-cosmos governance and law permission upgrade) and Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm (Myriad Races&#39; origin-balanced symbiotic ultimate form), reserving space for the realm system&#39;s infinite expansion.</p><h2 id="vi-common-iron-rules-of-the-four-sacred-cultivation-realms" tabindex="-1">VI. Common Iron Rules of the Four Sacred-Cultivation Realms <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-common-iron-rules-of-the-four-sacred-cultivation-realms" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Common Iron Rules of the Four Sacred-Cultivation Realms&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Qualitative leaps cannot be skipped</strong>: every realm is an existence-dimensional leap, cannot be skipped by energy stacking</li><li><strong>Mind-state synchronized assessment</strong>: every realm breakthrough must pass ethical review, power and Dao heart must be in sync</li><li><strong>Responsibility increases with realm</strong>: the higher the realm, the heavier the public responsibility; Origin Realm strong ones spend at least 30% of time annually on public affairs</li><li><strong>Results shared network-wide</strong>: sacred strong ones&#39; cultivation insights, law understanding, and world-creation designs all connect to the Alaya Network</li><li><strong>Permanently monitorable</strong>: Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision monitor sacred strong ones throughout, preventing power abuse</li></ul><h2 id="vii-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">VII. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#vii-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VII. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Universal infinite backstop</strong>: the universal equal infinite law establishes that every being inherently possesses basic infinite power; the easygoing have a guarantee, strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose, predation naturally loses meaning</li><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: the four sacred-cultivation realms&#39; qualitative leap relies on law understanding and Dao-heart sublimation, not energy stacking; every realm breakthrough&#39;s energy consumption is far less than predatory cultivation&#39;s energy waste</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: sacred strong ones&#39; law permissions are tools for serving Myriad Races, not weapons for predation; Predatory Faction cultivators even if power meets standards cannot integrate Dao due to &quot;Dao-heart rejection&quot;</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo systems lock the ceiling at the fierce realm; the four sacred-cultivation realms in Heng Yuan Zhou are Myriad Races civilization&#39;s advanced goal, the 20% Activation Strategy is batch-cultivating Origin Realm strong ones</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the four sacred-cultivation realms set no race limits; every Myriad Races group has its own grandmasters, plane strong ones, world-creators, and Transcendents</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: the four sacred-cultivation realms&#39; law understanding and world-creation designs are all openly shared, laying the foundation for the Multiverse Realm and Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm&#39;s infinite expansion</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The four sacred-cultivation realms are not &quot;stronger power,&quot; but &quot;heavier responsibility.&quot; From Dao Integration to Origin, every realm&#39;s qualitative leap accompanies expansion of freedom and deepening of constraint. In predatory-faction systems, high realm means greater predation right; in the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, high realm means greater service obligation. This is the true meaning of &quot;sacred&quot; — not above beings, but bearing beings&#39; weight.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./14-修炼境界统一划分.html">14-Unified Cultivation Realm Classification</a> · <a href="./17-位面至高强者标准.html">17-Plane Transcendent Standards</a> · <a href="./03-共生文明宪章.html">03-Symbiotic Civilization Charter</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',33)])])}const g=a(r,[["render",o]]);export{m as __pageData,g as default};
